e vacuum energy, and what could this imply for a conditional formulation of the cosmological constant problem?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0087"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:16ec78f3c53eff2e8dd86bcdb932c832baa1ab164c91cc80955eb34726a13944","title":"Can perturbative breakdown of axion–tower interactions define an axion species scale whose comparison with the gravitational species scale yields an axion-WGC-like bound, and what conditional consequences follow for black-hole PQ-charge reduction?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0089"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:16e10c0da2d841f4ffd5ed48e3b7bc77117f06e63657539e9986e0fdd40455aa","title":"How does an axion change extremal dyonic black-hole mass relations and the connection between long-range forces and binding energies? Can interactions between non-identical states reveal possible UV constraints beyond conjectures formulated for self-forces?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0092"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:16d93eb3857131bec4e3b3cd591826de04780f5a98dd093e702b90d9e2caad71","title":"Which leading gravitational couplings of a massive spin-2 supermultiplet are compatible with undeformed four-dimensional N=1 supergravity, and what do they imply for an isolated massive spin-2 effective theory?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0092"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:165375343c45408d576a510b6170ea017d24a98c3b357791332dee927a0bc424","title":"Under specified brane boundary conditions, how does the bulk scalar potential determine whether the radion stabilizes, and can geometric brane-world sum rules estimate the stabilized interbrane separation?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0094"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:16e651